  "headline": "FDA lists dopamine hydrochloride injection as a current shortage first posted 2017-11-06; Baxter, Hikma, and Hospira are all listed as Current with recent updates in October 2026.",
  "headline_cites": ["E22", "E19", "E20", "E21"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows dopamine hydrochloride injection as Current with an initial posting date of 2017-11-06 and an update date of 2026-10-16 for Baxter Healthcare.",
      "cites": ["E22", "E19"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. is also listed as Current with an initial posting date of 2017-11-06 and an update date of 2026-10-14, noting the product is temporarily on backorder with additional lots expected in the February 2027 timeframe.",
      "cites": ["E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc., a Pfizer Company, is listed as Current with an initial posting date of 2017-11-06 and an update date of 2026-10-08.",
      "cites": ["E21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 108 months.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The preferred alternate per P&T interchange is dopamine hydrochloride 40 mg/mL from Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc., approved by Alex Morgan, PharmD on 2025-10-24, with a requirement to recalculate dose and volume and obtain pharmacist verification.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E23"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A second alternate is dopamine hydrochloride 40 mg/mL from Hospira, Inc., approved by Alex Morgan, PharmD on 2025-12-19, with the same recalculation and verification requirements.",
      "cites": ["D8", "E24"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Current on-hand supply across Corvale sites ranges from 11.7 to 13.8 days at present usage rates.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D3"]
    }
  ]
}
